            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-IRLTdflBuomn9axVt1ClniXfgxg\">Overall, Congo and Nigeria maintained their positions as the largest oil producers throughout the period. Chad and Somalia saw significant growth in their output while Congo experienced a steady decline in its production, and Nigeria's figures fluctuated during these years.</div>\n</div>",
