            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-CcR0d27uxoHDQ3xhQGHlydBJg1g\">Looking at the major oil-producing nations, Congo led the group with 275,000 barrels per day in 2000, which was 70,000 barrels higher than Nigeria's output. Congo's production subsequently decreased year by year, falling to 203,000 barrels daily by 2004. Meanwhile, Nigeria's figures showed some variation, dropping to 190,000 barrels in 2002 before recovering to reach 213,000 barrels per day in the final year.</div>\n</div>",
