          {
            "id": 522,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-S5RidvIEVoL3KhxKVF3lARGzgFf\">Regarding the remaining countries, both Chad and Somalia started with minimal production, at zero and 5,000 barrels per day respectively in 2000. Chad's output remained unchanged until 2003, when it began producing 8,000 barrels daily, before surging to 50,000 barrels in 2004. Similarly, Somalia's production rose consistently throughout the period, increasing more than tenfold from its initial figure to match Chad's output of 50,000 barrels per day by 2004.</div>\n</div>",
